    ]
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Golf organiser Seymour Marvin helped create the Brazilian Golf Association so the country could send a team to the first World Amateur Team Championship. Working with Oswaldo Aranha and Carlos Borges, he provided a national organisation for international competition. He captained Brazil's inaugural team at St Andrews and continued leading its delegations for decades.\n\nMarvin never played in the championship itself. At the inaugural meeting, however, he won a separate handicap competition for non-playing captains, delegates and officials. His Delegates and Duffers Cup victory placed him ahead of the presidents of the Canadian and United States golf associations.",
    "html": "<p>Golf organiser Seymour Marvin helped create the Brazilian Golf Association so the country could send a team to the first World Amateur Team Championship. Working with Oswaldo Aranha and Carlos Borges, he provided a national organisation for international competition. He captained Brazil's inaugural team at St Andrews and continued leading its delegations for decades.</p>\r\n<p>Marvin never played in the championship itself. At the inaugural meeting, however, he won a separate handicap competition for non-playing captains, delegates and officials. His Delegates and Duffers Cup victory placed him ahead of the presidents of the Canadian and United States golf associations.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 98,
